Lexius Help / File Reference
----------------------------

File Access (Electron + Web)
- Electron: preload.js exposes fs.readFile / fs.writeFile via IPC; main.js handles channels
- Web: web-api.js / web.js serve REST endpoints at /api/files (read/write/delete/list)
- Web frontend: fs class in assets/scripts/langs.js.js uses File System Access API first, then REST fallback; API_BASE = window.location.origin
- db.js sync: IndexedDB + filesystem sync; web saves also push to REST API; getFile falls back to API if DB missing

Prompt System (built-in, replaces browser prompt())
- PromptModal({ title, placeholder, defaultValue, onSubmit, onCancel }) -> modal for workspace names / other inputs (used in navbar.js)
- Prompt(message, placeholder) -> direct input in file list for file/folder creation (used in langs.js.js newFile/newFolder)

File / Folder Creation & Opening
- newFile / newFileCtx: await Prompt('Enter new file name', '') -> creates file, sets icon, saves empty content
- newFolderCtx: await Prompt('Enter folder name', '') -> creates folder
- File click on .filesContainer -> openSelectedFile() -> getFile() -> initEditor()
- Open Folder button (id: open-folder) -> showDirectoryPicker() -> window.dirHandle set
- Rename: right-click -> renameFile -> inline input -> save

Project Files
assets/images -> icons/images
assets/scripts -> frontend JS (db.js, langs.js.js, monaco.js, preload.js, theme.js, navbar.js)
assets/scripts/langs.js.js -> main UI, file mgmt, Prompt(), fs class, editor init
assets/scripts/db.js -> IndexedDB wrapper with Electron/web filesystem sync
assets/scripts/preload.js -> Electron contextBridge (window control + fs)
assets/scripts/monaco.js -> Monaco editor loader
assets/scripts/theme.js -> theme switcher
assets/scripts/navbar.js -> navbar dropdown, workspace creation (PromptModal), folder picker
assets/styles -> CSS
assets/themes -> Monaco theme files

Web Server
- web.js: combined static + file API server (port 3456 by default, WORKSPACE_DIR = web-workspace/)
- web-api.js: standalone REST file API server
- package.json: scripts include start, desktop, web, web:api, build

Update Log
update-log.txt -> changes per version
version -> current version
